WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.850
- You're busy with,
like, this amazing record

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:03.690
that I'm very excited about.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:04.797
I got to sing on it.

00:00:04.797 --> 00:00:06.000
(audience cheering)

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.890
I got to sing on it.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.410
And, I'm very excited for ya'll to hear it

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.040
because I only got to hear
the songs you let me hear,

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:11.873
that I was singing on.

00:00:11.873 --> 00:00:13.630
And then I got the record and I just,

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:17.810
literally, you never fail
to impress me with like,

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.740
your voice, it's insane.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.733
Like literally, like it's
insane how talented you are.

00:00:22.733 --> 00:00:23.566
- Thank you for saying that.

00:00:23.566 --> 00:00:24.630
- Like, your record is amazing

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:25.463
and you know what I love about it

00:00:25.463 --> 00:00:26.710
is you stick to country music.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.080
It sounds like country music that we love.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.510
- Well, it's what I grew up
on, I mean, it's what I love,

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:32.010
it's the music that I was influenced by.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.410
I'm a big Linda Ronstadt fan,
- Yes.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:38.010
and that stuff has fiddles
and steel guitars all over it.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.240
- She crossed genres, yeah.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.140
Yeah, yeah, yeah, that was really cool.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.380
- Totally. So, I'm not a
traditional country singer,

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.310
but I definitely fall
in the country category.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.410
And I just want to tell you guys,

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.610
when Kelly came in to sing on the record,

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:49.020
I've been in every interview
I've been doing this week

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:50.220
about the album release.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.850
I'm like, what is it about
Kelly? I'm like, she's not real,

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:54.005
like, she's not normal,
like, she's just amazing.

00:00:54.005 --> 00:00:55.640
- (laughs) She's crazy.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.620
- And she comes in and she just, you know,

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.160
I hear this high strong harmony

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.400
and I know I'm not going to sing it,

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.233
and I'm like, Kelly,

00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:02.760
can you come over here and do this for me?

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.410
And it's just amazing what you bring.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.360
And I know you could probably,

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.370
everyone you sing with you
make them sound better,

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:08.840
but I love our voices together.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.620
- Oh my god, I do too!
- I love singing with you.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.615
- Yeah, let's do more.

00:01:11.615 --> 00:01:12.448
- Let's do more.

00:01:12.448 --> 00:01:13.489
(laughs)
(audience cheering)

00:01:13.489 --> 00:01:14.806
What's funny is after the first one

00:01:14.806 --> 00:01:16.670
we got to record together
was "PrizeFighter."

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:20.100
And I got there and I had no idea

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.258
that her husband was going
to be, like, producing it.

00:01:22.258 --> 00:01:23.250
(laughs)

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.900
And I was like, "Uhhh." (laughs)

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.860
And I got in the studio,
and I'll tell you,

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.760
I've never been more
nervous about sounding good

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.950
because I was like, you're there already,

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.250
that was nerve wracking enough.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.480
And then your husband who's, you know,

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.438
Garth fricking Brooks
walks in and he's like--

00:01:38.438 --> 00:01:40.686
(audience cheering)

00:01:40.686 --> 00:01:43.470
And literally he was producing me.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.119
I was peeing my pants.

00:01:45.119 --> 00:01:45.952
(laughs)

00:01:45.952 --> 00:01:48.350
I was like, this is the
worst. But anyway, I--

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.810
- He was trolling my session

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:50.643
to try to get you to work with him.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:51.476
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:51.476 --> 00:01:52.385
- That's totally what
he was doing. (laughs)

00:01:52.385 --> 00:01:54.770
Well, I was literally about to die

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:56.580
'cause I was so nervous! Both of you!

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.147
I mean you're just such this
power couple and it's like,

00:01:59.147 --> 00:01:59.980
"Uhhh"
- Oh, please.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:01.454
If you go back and listen to
the end of "PrizeFighter,"

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.290
I don't know if you remember
this at the end we were,

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:04.360
there were these licks at the end,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.300
and so we were kind of doing
these answers to each other.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.350
And I remember that I had
done something and you went in

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:09.407
and then you did your lick and I'm like,

00:02:09.407 --> 00:02:10.510
"Let me go back in there." (sniffles)

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:11.343
Like, give me another shot at it.

00:02:11.343 --> 00:02:12.176
(laughs)

00:02:12.176 --> 00:02:13.220
And so, I went back in and did it again,

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.507
and then Kelly said,
"Let me go back in there

00:02:14.507 --> 00:02:15.470
"and give it another shot." (laughs)

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:18.210
- I was very nervous. But
he's actually really cool.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:20.540
I was wondering, does he ever
crash your girls' nights?

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.373
Does he--
- He doesn't--

00:02:21.373 --> 00:02:22.206
- 'Cause he seems funny like that.

00:02:22.206 --> 00:02:24.400
- He's a little afraid of
that many women together,

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.688
so he really doesn't,

00:02:25.688 --> 00:02:28.300
but if he's around he'll open the wine.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.440
But he really wants to be gone, like,

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.621
I think it scares him a little bit.

00:02:31.621 --> 00:02:32.454
- Really?

00:02:32.454 --> 00:02:33.420
- As it should, you know.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.253
- Women, a bunch of women.

00:02:34.253 --> 00:02:35.086
(laughs)

00:02:35.086 --> 00:02:37.320
- And here's something else
about you men! (laughs)

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.153
No, doesn't. Yeah (laughs)

00:02:38.153 --> 00:02:40.485
- It's like a designing
women episode (laughs)

00:02:40.485 --> 00:02:42.770
You're ruining everything! (laughs)

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:43.620
That's amazing.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.040
Okay so, I know that
whatever you cook sometimes,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.400
you're a fabulous cook. She is.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.435
I've gone to her house she makes--

00:02:48.435 --> 00:02:50.310
(audience cheering)

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:51.660
And she gives you wine!

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.310
It's the most amazing experience.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.730
But one thing I found out
actually was the fact that when,

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:56.900
he cooks sometimes, right?

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:57.733
Garth cooks sometimes?
- He does. He does.

00:02:57.733 --> 00:03:01.310
- Okay. And he he's like, very
perfectionist at it, right?

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:02.640
He's pretty good, right?

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.240
- He's pretty good. I
wouldn't say perfectionist.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.940
He doesn't follow a recipe,
he pretty much like,

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.910
will throw things together
that maybe go together,

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.551
and then he thinks it's fabulous
and takes a picture of it.

00:03:10.551 --> 00:03:11.920
(laughs)

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:13.644
I call him "Gartha Stewart" because he's--

00:03:13.644 --> 00:03:15.837
- (laughs) That's amazing!

00:03:15.837 --> 00:03:19.070
That's (mumbles) I love that
you call him Gartha Stewart!

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.370
- He's very impressed, like
look I made this sandwich,

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.410
I took a picture of it, and I'm
like, that's awesome, honey.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:23.420
- Yeah, and you're like,

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.200
meanwhile, you're like
look I have a cooking show

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.200
and I'm badass at it (laughs)

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.537
- Well, but I'll be like,

00:03:27.537 --> 00:03:28.710
"Can you open this jar of pickles?"

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:29.840
And like, "Well, I have
my own cooking show."

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:30.936
I'm like, really? Seriously?

00:03:30.936 --> 00:03:31.769
(laughs)

00:03:31.769 --> 00:03:32.602
- Stay in your lane!

00:03:32.602 --> 00:03:33.477
- Right!
- Gartha!

00:03:33.477 --> 00:03:34.310
(laughs)

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.170
I just found that amazing.
I found that amazing.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.520
So here's the thing, I
love the "Every Girl."

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:41.410
Like, tell me why you chose
that name for your record,

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.560
that song, like tell me, where
did "Every Girl" come from?

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:44.860
- The truth is--
- I love it.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:46.010
- Thank you very much. The truth is,

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:46.843
well you are every girl.

00:03:46.843 --> 00:03:47.676
(laughs)

00:03:47.676 --> 00:03:50.980
The truth is that I went in
to make a record for fun.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.780
I'm 54 years old, I'm a woman.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.850
My expectations of what was
going to happen with this record

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:56.540
were not super high, (laughs)

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.510
so I was just like, I just
want to make a record I love.

00:03:58.510 --> 00:03:59.980
And I wasn't thinking about singles.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:02.031
I wasn't thinking about radio, at all.

00:04:02.031 --> 00:04:02.864
- That's what we should be doing.

00:04:02.864 --> 00:04:03.697
- Which is what we should be doing.

00:04:03.697 --> 00:04:04.900
If you want to call yourself an artist,

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.290
you make art and that's what you do.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:07.960
And then you figure
out what to do with it.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:10.230
And, this song was one of
the first ones I heard,

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.800
and I just liked it. I liked what it said.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.027
Basically, it has a line that says,

00:04:13.027 --> 00:04:14.860
"You got this, baby,
so what if you don't."

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:16.610
I love that line because it's like,

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.270
we're always trying to be so perfect

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.687
and it's really nice when we're told,

00:04:19.687 --> 00:04:20.900
"It's okay to not be perfect."

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:21.752
- Yeah.

00:04:21.752 --> 00:04:24.080
- And then, it just kind
of, when my team heard it,

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.450
they were like, "We're going
to radio and this is the song."

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:27.740
And I've been more shocked than anybody

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:28.660
that it's getting played on the radio,

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:31.200
which it is, so I'm like, "Woohoo!"

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.260
- That's what I love about your record.

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:34.070
It sounds country, it's what
it's supposed to be like,

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:36.570
and, honestly in this
time in country music,

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:37.763
like I grew up in the '90s,

00:04:37.763 --> 00:04:40.620
like listening to music,
there were so many of ya'll!

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.430
There were so many great,
like, country women.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.500
And like, right now, it's
hard just to be a woman,

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:45.680
to get played on country music,

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.430
and then you're saying, "Oh, I'm 54."

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:48.822
It's hard to do that at 54 to get played.

00:04:48.822 --> 00:04:50.620
- Right, right. It's
just all these layers of,

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.330
and I don't understand that
either because people think,

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:54.480
well maybe country music is just behind.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.826
But in the '90s, there were
so many female artists.

00:04:56.826 --> 00:04:58.670
- Oh my gosh, I could name a plethora!

00:04:58.670 --> 00:04:59.503
- Yeah.

00:04:59.503 --> 00:05:01.330
- So what happened? I have
this conversation all the time

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:04.300
with all the girls I know
in country music, I'm like,

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:05.170
what's happening?

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.203
- I think it's my fault. I
left town, I moved to Oklahoma

00:05:07.203 --> 00:05:08.036
for 14 years.
- Yeah, why did you ruin it?

00:05:08.036 --> 00:05:09.033
Why did she ruin it?

00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:10.493
- (laughs) I ruin everything.

00:05:10.493 --> 00:05:13.790
(audience clapping)

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:15.960
When I moved to Oklahoma
and married Garth,

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.880
and we raised the girls,
and then when we came back,

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:20.899
I was shocked! I was like,
what has happened? I know--

00:05:20.899 --> 00:05:21.920
- There's like two that are played.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.540
- Right. And I don't
really know the answer.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:26.120
I do know that living in Nashville now,

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.220
the girls have kind of banded together.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.850
And it's been really cool
to see generationally,

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.050
like, the young girls who grew up

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.070
on "She's In Love With The
Boy," and then my generation,

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:35.290
and then we've got Reba and Loretta.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.450
Everybody's, kind of, this girl club,

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:40.837
and the conversations now
being had out loud and loudly,

00:05:40.837 --> 00:05:43.447
and the men in our
industry who support that,

00:05:43.447 --> 00:05:47.600
like Garth and Blake and Luke,
who have spoken out about it,

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:48.670
that's when change happens.

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:51.630
So, I think, right now,
everybody's just being really loud.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:53.650
The CMAs this year are going
to be hosted by three women

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:54.930
for the first time in
the history of the CMAs.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:55.763
(audience cheering)

00:05:55.763 --> 00:05:58.230
- Is it Carrie, with Reba and Dolly?

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.063
- Yeah.

00:05:59.063 --> 00:05:59.896
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:05:59.896 --> 00:06:02.127
And it isn't against the
men, it's not saying that.

00:06:02.127 --> 00:06:04.850
It's just saying, we're here,
we're not going anywhere.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:06.480
- Yeah. But let's team up!
Let's make beautiful music.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:07.937
Let's make something happen.

